PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H}

The least plausible option is H. It fabricates an unsupported link between the Kuji-in hand seals, “nine holes” Taoist erotics, and yin-yang rituals that have no basis in the Bansenshukai, in documented ninjutsu sources, or in period Japanese practice; the other choices, while speculative, at least stay within attested historical mechanisms (redaction, moral censorship, physical wear, or invisible-ink conventions) that could plausibly produce uniform blanks across copies. 

(The historical Bansenshukai does contain a kunoichi section, but the “missing kanji” motif itself appears to be a modern puzzle device rather than a documented textual feature; that does not change the relative plausibility ranking among the given options.)

